REALITY: accept a Client Hello without X25519MLKEM768.

Since XTLS/REALITY 8cdf7bf9 such a hello never authenticates and is handed to
the target. sing-box removes that group from its hello and mihomo does by
default, and older Xray clients don't send it, so all of them reach the
inbound but carry nothing. Clients still have to prove the key, and a prober
without it still gets the target as before.

--- a/tls.go
+++ b/tls.go
@@ -231,9 +231,6 @@
 					break // ensure order
 				}
 			}
-			if peerPub2 == nil {
-				break // reject outdated/strange Client Hello that doesn't have X25519MLKEM768 before optional X25519
-			}
 			if peerPub == nil {
 				peerPub = peerPub2 // secondary choice: X25519 in X25519MLKEM768
 			}
